      "math_academy_id": "q-127692",
      "sequence_position": 5,
      "problem": "Consider the curve $r(t)=⟨3\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t,\\,2-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t⟩,$ $t\\ge 0,$ for which the arc length $s$ from $r(0)$ to $r(t)$ is given by $s=12t.$ Find $R(s),$ the parametrization of the curve by its arc length $s.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, since $s=12t,$ we have that $t=\\frac{s}{12}.$\n\nThe vector function that pametrizes the curve $r(t)$ by its arc length $s,$ with $s\\ge 0,$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\frac{s}{12}) \\\\  & =⟨3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\cdot \\frac{s}{12}),\\,2-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\cdot \\frac{s}{12})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{3}),\\,2-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{3})⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields_complete": true,
